{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-ext-deriv","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:categorical-q-ext-deriv","kind":"definition","title":"Categorical $q$-deformed exterior derivative","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-connection","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-positive-definite-dagger"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-ext-deriv","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-lie-bracket","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-connection","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-vector-field","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-flow","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-torsion-leaf"],"tags":["exterior-derivative","deformation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv","text":"categorical-q-ext-deriv.md","leanSource":"categorical-q-ext-deriv.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"def:categorical-q-ext-deriv\"></a>\n<strong>Definition.</strong> <em>Categorical <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed exterior derivative</em></p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed exterior derivative</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q \\colon \\Omega^k(A) \\to \\Omega^{k+1}(A)</code> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  d_q =  q^{-1}d + (1 - q^{-1})\\pi_V \\circ d,</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d \\colon \\Omega^k(A) \\to \\Omega^{k+1}(A)</code> is the differential of the non-commutative de Rham complex. The operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q</code> acts as <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^{-1}d</code> on horizontal forms and as <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d</code> on vertical forms. The <em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-adjoint</em> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\delta_q \\colon \\Omega^{k+1}(A) \\to \\Omega^k(A)</code> is the formal adjoint of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q</code> with respect to the dagger structure. These operators exist and are unique.</p>\n"}
